{
  "title": "LED controller enclosure",
  "summary": "A screw-together PETG case for an 8-output LED controller board: base with 16 panel-connector holes, an Ethernet slot, antenna and power holes and vents, a lid with a vent grille, and a small test strip to pick the connector hole size first.",
  "status": "preview",
  "date": "2026-11-03",
  "material": "PETG",
  "notes": "Modelled in the LED controller project (dig_octa_case.py); this desk only slices and prints. All three parts are placed as designed: flat side on the bed, no supports. PETG (the case sits next to a 300 W power supply), 0.2 mm layers, 4 walls (M3 screws self-tap into 2.6 mm holes), 20 % gyroid infill. Test fit: three connector holes, 15.0 / 15.4 / 15.8 mm, numbers engraved; print it first and pick the hole that fits, since the base's 16 holes use that size. Lid: outside face on the bed, lip up, countersinks open on the bed side; printed on TNT at 255 °C with flow capped at 8 mm³/s for its weak hot end. Base: 7 h 52 min, 5 mm brim, on Gås once the hole size is settled; the slicer turns it 90° on the bed, and it stays clear of the cutter corner.",
